      "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}4}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}3$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/0f7c5ff7155c00a811c744606ee039e764c6ded16f214a163b6d5d4a481e633b.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{6}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{24}.\n$$",
